[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ZEF WHY — user problems and needs
UID: ZEF-WHY-DOC
VERSION: 1.0.0
DATE: 2026-10-10
PREFIX: ZEF-WHY
ROOT: True
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
WHY items describe the problems and user needs that motivate ZEF. They define
intent only: no solution, system boundary, API, or implementation is assumed.
Each WHAT item refines one or more WHY items.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Predictable embedded behavior

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-001
TITLE: Reliable event-driven coordination
STATEMENT: Developers of small embedded products need independent pieces of application behavior to coordinate predictably on limited processors.
COMMENT: User need: coordinate independent behavior while keeping the execution model understandable.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-002
TITLE: Predictable resource use
STATEMENT: Embedded application developers need framework memory requirements to be predictable at build time on resource-constrained devices.
COMMENT: User need: calculate the framework storage required before deployment.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-003
TITLE: Controlled design process
STATEMENT: >>>
Project maintainers need a foundation whose design follows a defined, formal process that ensures clear requirements and traceability to specifications and tests.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
User need: adopt and distribute the result with clear ownership and an auditable design origin.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Application modeling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-010
TITLE: Understandable domain vocabulary
STATEMENT: Application developers need a small, consistent vocabulary for describing independent application behavior across documentation, interfaces, and tests.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-011
TITLE: Safe message sharing
STATEMENT: Application developers need to pass data among independent consumers and know exactly when that data can be changed or reclaimed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-012
TITLE: Composable hierarchical behavior
STATEMENT: Application developers need to model nested modes of behavior with deterministic handling, entry, exit, and transition behavior.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-013
TITLE: Bounded component lifecycle
STATEMENT: Application developers need independent pieces of behavior with explicit ownership for the lifetime of the application.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-014
TITLE: Deferred local work
STATEMENT: Application developers need to retain incoming work until a component reaches a state where it can process it, without losing or duplicating that work.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scheduling and time

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-020
TITLE: Deterministic scheduling
STATEMENT: Application developers need predictable ordering and bounded units of application work that can be exercised on a host.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-021
TITLE: Topic fanout
STATEMENT: Application developers need one occurrence of application information to reach every interested consumer without multiplying storage.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-022
TITLE: Time-based delivery
STATEMENT: Application developers need delayed and repeating behavior while preserving responsiveness to other application work.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-023
TITLE: Portable concurrency boundary
STATEMENT: Platform developers need a well-defined boundary between normal application execution and asynchronous hardware activity.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-024
TITLE: Future preemption without semantic drift
STATEMENT: Product developers need to introduce stronger responsiveness or execution overlap later without changing behavior already understood by applications.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Adoption and verification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-030
TITLE: Verifiable adoption
STATEMENT: Maintainers need public behavior, configuration limits, and verification evidence to remain connected as the framework evolves.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-WHY-031
TITLE: Licensing
STATEMENT: >>>
The framework needs to be permissively licensed to allow both commercial and open-source use.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
